/-!
# The genuine smooth-function sheaf and its proved fine structure

The real smooth complex-function sheaf is constructed from actual
bundled smooth maps.  Actual global multipliers supply its complex
scalar action, and a genuine smooth partition of unity proves its
finite fine property on finite-dimensional, Hausdorff, sigma-compact
smooth real manifolds.  In particular the topological hypotheses hold
for compact Hausdorff smooth manifolds.

This package does not identify the smooth sheaf with the holomorphic
sheaf, and does not assume analytic cohomology vanishing.
-/
